# text = Hyde was pale and dwarfish , he gave an impression of deformity without any nameable malformation , he had a displeasing smile , he had borne himself to the lawyer with a sort of murderous mixture of timidity and boldness , and he spoke with a husky , whispering and somewhat broken voice ; all these were points against him , but not all of these together could explain the hitherto unknown disgust , loathing , and fear with which Mr . Utterson regarded him said the perplexed gentleman Round the corner from the by-street , there was a square of ancient , handsome houses , now for the most part decayed from their high estate and let in flats and chambers to all sorts and conditions of men : map-engravers , architects , shady lawyers , and the agents of obscure enterprises .
