# text = And yet when Utterson remarked on his ill-looks , it was with an air of greatness that Lanyon declared himself a doomed man he said observed Utterson But Lanyon's face changed , and he held up a trembling hand he said in a loud , unsteady voice said Mr . Utterson ; and then after a considerable pause he inquired returned Lanyon said the lawyer was the reply As soon as he got home , Utterson sat down and wrote to Jekyll , complaining of his exclusion from the house , and asking the cause of this unhappy break with Lanyon ; and the next day brought him a long answer , often very pathetically worded , and sometimes darkly mysterious in drift .
