# text = That part of me which I had the power of projecting , had lately been much exercised and nourished ; it had seemed to me of late as though the body of Edward Hyde had grown in stature , as though ( when I wore that form ) I were conscious of a more generous tide of blood ; and I began to spy a danger that , if this were much prolonged , the balance of my nature might be permanently overthrown , the power of voluntary change be forfeited , and the character of Edward Hyde become irrevocably mine .
